  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nIt's another clear morning across much of the country with only\na few cirrus clouds streaming across the northern Plains and \nnorthern MN. South winds remain occasionally gusty and is\nhelping keep temperatures mild in the mid 40s to lower 50s. A\nfront will approach this afternoon from the northwest which will\nallow winds to drop off across central MN. Gusty winds will\ncontinue across southern MN and WI into afternoon. 925 mb temps\nwill range from +13 to +15C this afternoon, which would equate\nto highs in the upper 60s, with a few low 70s across \nsouthwestern MN.\n\nAfter slightly cooler temperatures Monday, a warming trend is\nexpected to prevail through the rest of the week. The pattern \nwill feature a ridge across much of the CONUS with troughs on \nthe east and west coasts. Very quiet and warm weather will \nresult, and temperatures well into the 70s are expected from\nmidweek onward. A few 80s possible late week. Normal highs by \nthen will be in the low to mid 50s, which makes this forecast \n15 to 25 degrees above normal. Highs through the period were \nweighted toward the NBM 90th percentile given the recent cool \nbias of the NBM. \n\nThe only chances for rain come next weekend as the western long\nwave trough finally begins to approach. However, recent trends \nhave been bringing this front through drier and it is not \nlooking like we'll have widespread meaningful precipitation.",
